* DATA creates the ACCOUNT constructor and a field selector, BAL, that can be assigned to.
* DEPOSIT updates the record passed as A by assigning through BAL(A).
* The caller can read BAL(A) directly because the field selector is available outside the function.
    DATA('ACCOUNT(BAL)')
    DEFINE('DEPOSIT(A,N)')
    A = ACCOUNT(5)
    DEPOSIT(A,2)
    OUTPUT = BAL(A) :(END)
DEPOSIT BAL(A) = BAL(A) + N :(RETURN)
END
